{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 73,
          "w": 456
        },
        "text": "World normal / view direction for the fresnel, mesh UV for the hex grid and the OBJECT-space position for the ripple distance."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_rim",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 762
        },
        "text": "The shared **Fresnel Rim Kit**: `(1 − N·V)^power`, scaled by *Rim Strength*. The rim makes the shield read as a volume."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_hex",
        "position": {
          "x": 682,
          "y": 494
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 3296
        },
        "text": "`uv × (2, 1)` keeps the hexagons round on a 2:1 UV sphere. *Edge* is 0 in the cell centre and 1 on the border, so the outline is `smoothstep(1 − width, 1, edge)`. Every cell gets a random phase from a hash of its ID, so the fills pulse out of sync. The sum is weighted by `0.25 + rim`: the grid shows mostly towards the silhouette."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_ripple",
        "position": {
          "x": 4182,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 3602
        },
        "text": "Time since the hit is `T` (the *Hit Time* parameter, or a looping sawtooth when *Auto Hit* is on). The wavefront radius is `T × speed`; the ring is `1 − smoothstep(0, width, |distance(pos, hitPos) − radius|)` and it fades with `1 − T / life`. Inside the ring the hex outlines flash brighter (`ring × (0.6 + 1.6 × line)`), which makes the wave read as travelling through the grid."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_color",
        "position": {
          "x": 7988,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "`base = rim + grid`; colour = (`shield × base + hit × ripple`) × intensity, alpha = saturate(base + ripple). The ripple has its own HDR colour so a hit reads as a different energy from the idle shield."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 9652,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Additive blend, ZWrite off, two-sided."
      }
    ],
